<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Dar Sila</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1916 CE (approx.) · capital Goz Beida</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Daju sultanate in south-eastern Chad, heir to the old Daju kings of Darfur, that kept its autonomy between Wadai and Darfur until 1916.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Daju had ruled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> before the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tunjur-kingdom">Tunjur</a>, as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/daju-kingdom">Daju kingdom</a>. Their royal line later moved south-west to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sila-region">Sila</a> region, in present-day south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a>, where by the mid-17th century they had established a sultanate, eventually based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goz-beida">Goz Beida</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Dar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sila-region">Sila</a>'s sultans ruled a farming population in a well-watered savanna region and controlled hunting and slave-raiding zones to the south. The sultanate paid tribute at times to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a> or the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a> but retained its own dynasty. Few details of its government are recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the French conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a>, the sultan of Dar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sila-region">Sila</a> resisted, and French forces occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goz-beida">Goz Beida</a> in 1916. The sultanate became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chad-french-colony">Chad (French colony)</a>, and its sultans continued as traditional rulers.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1650 CE – 1916 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0